msgid ""
"Add one or more new fields to an existing IvyForms form. This ability "
"modifies stored form configuration \n"
"                (writes the whole form payload like the builder save). "
"REQUIRED INPUTS: formId and fields (each item requires type). \n"
"                Optional per-field keys mirror add-form-field. SUPPORTED "
"FIELD TYPES: text, textarea, email, number, phone, website, name, radio, "
"checkbox, select, multi-select, address, date, time, rating, html. If "
"IvyForms Pro is active, password and signature fields are also supported. "
"IMPORTANT WORKFLOW RULES: 1. This ability ONLY adds fields to an existing "
"form (it does NOT create a form). 2. If formId is missing or unknown, the "
"agent MUST first use get-forms or \n"
"                create-form before calling this. 3. After successfully "
"adding fields, the next step should usually be open-form-builder\n"
"                 so the user can review layout and options. 4. Do not assume "
"field ordering unless explicitly returned by the API response. FIELD "
"BEHAVIOR NOTES: - label defaults to a capitalized version of type if not "
"provided. - required defaults to false. - width defaults to 100 if not "
"specified. - description is helper text shown under the field in UI. COMMON "
"AGENT MISTAKES TO AVOID: - Do NOT call this if the user wants to create a "
"form (use create-form instead). - Do NOT assume the field already exists "
"after calling this ability until API confirms success. - Do NOT duplicate "
"fields manually; use duplicate-form-field for that purpose."
msgstr ""
"Añade uno o más campos nuevos a un formulario de IvyForms existente. Esta "
"capacidad modifica la configuración del formulario almacenada \n"
"                (escribe toda la carga útil del formulario, como al guardar "
"en el constructor). REQUIRED INPUTS: formId and fields (each item requires "
"type). \n"
"                Las claves opcionales por campo reflejan add-form-field. "
"SUPPORTED FIELD TYPES: text, textarea, email, number, phone, website, name, "
"radio, checkbox, select, multi-select, address, date, time, rating, html. Si "
"IvyForms Pro está activo, también se admiten los campos password y "
"signature. IMPORTANT WORKFLOW RULES: 1. Esta capacidad ONLY añade campos a "
"un formulario existente (no crea un formulario). 2. Si falta formId o es "
"desconocido, el agente MUST usar primero get-forms o \n"
"                create-form antes de llamar a esto. 3. Tras añadir campos "
"correctamente, el siguiente paso normalmente debería ser open-form-builder\n"
"                 para que la persona usuaria pueda revisar el diseño y las "
"opciones. 4. No asumas el orden de los campos a menos que la respuesta de la "
"API lo devuelva explícitamente. FIELD BEHAVIOR NOTES: - label usa por "
"defecto una versión de type con la primera letra en mayúscula si no se "
"proporciona. - required es false por defecto. - width es 100 por defecto si "
"no se especifica. - description es el texto de ayuda que se muestra debajo "
"del campo en la UI. COMMON AGENT MISTAKES TO AVOID: - Do NOT call this if "
"the user wants to create a form (use create-form instead). - Do NOT assume "
"the field already exists after calling this ability until API confirms "
"success. - Do NOT duplicate fields manually; use duplicate-form-field for "
"that purpose."

